DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       xxddgg--uusseerr--ddiirr looks up the current path for one of the special XDG user
       dirs.

       This command expects the name of an XDG user dir as argument. The
       possible names are:
           DESKTOP
           DOWNLOAD
           TEMPLATES
           PUBLICSHARE
           DOCUMENTS
           MUSIC
           PICTURES
           VIDEOS

FFIILLEESS
       The values are looked up in the user-dirs.dirs file. This file is
       created by the xdg-user-dirs-update utility.

